ut pub/sub is  it has essentially instantaneous  elasticity on the publishing side it'll  act as that surge tank right so if you  all of a sudden want to publish a  hundred thousand messages you can do  that it might fill up a queue and you  may not want to have you know 20 servers  standing by expensively waiting to  process them all but you have at least  you've at least handled the ingestion  instantaneously so certain things align  with performance and cost certain things  are not so IOT core and pops up you're  really build on bites you are not build  to have a faster byte transmitted so  there really isn't a extra cost  association associated with more  performance for things like IOT core or  pub/sub other services like BigTable if  you want more throughput and more  performance you actually do pay more for  more throughput right so there is a  there is a correlation there between  cost and performance memory is an  expensive thing right if you want to  have the performance of Redis for that  high speed counter you need to  essentially have RAM on hand for those  kind of operations so in general you  need to be optimizing not only for  performance and cost and you should be  looking at how the impact of increasing  performance increases your cost or where  you get performance essentially for free  that's built into the to the pricing  model  so in conclusion I think you know be  mindful of where performance actually  has impact the phrase premature  optimization is is real right if you're  worried about 20 milliseconds somewhere  on on a publishing speed but you have a  transmit time of 800 milliseconds over a  satellite link is that your biggest  concern at the moment right should you  be really trying to shave 2 or 3  milliseconds or microseconds off of  something on the device if it's really  just a rounding error in your end-to-end  latency so consider each of these layers  right so just to review the physical  layer what is the if you if you look at  som